  "releaseNotes": "**DI008 Named Type-Argument Precision**: DI008 now maps `serviceType:` and `implementationType:` by Roslyn parameter binding for non-generic `AddTransient(...)` / `AddKeyedTransient(...)` overloads, so out-of-order named arguments report the disposable implementation instead of trusting source order. | **DI008 Factory Guardrails**: Keyed transient factory registrations with named arguments out of order now stay quiet, preserving the rule's intentional factory-registration boundary.",
